# Prefer Cloud Agent Builds

Apply this rule when the task involves Cursor Cloud Agents, `.cursor/environment.json`, Cloud Agent Builds, install/start scripts, or speeding up remote agents.

## Builds over cold installs

- Put clone-time and dependency work in `.cursor/environment.json` `install` so **Builds** bake it once. Do not tell the agent to re-run a full install at the start of every cloud session unless lockfiles changed.
- `install` must be idempotent, non-interactive, and must exit. Use lockfile-accurate commands (`pnpm install --frozen-lockfile`, `npm ci`, `uv sync --frozen`, `go mod download`).
- Builds snapshot **disk**, not processes. Long-running services belong in `start` or `terminals` (for example `sudo service docker start`). Dev servers usually belong in AGENTS.md (`pnpm dev`), not in `install`.
- A committed `.cursor/environment.json` overrides personal/team dashboard environments for that repo. Change it carefully; diff before replacing a working file.
- After config changes, the human still needs to create or refresh the Cloud Agent environment so a Build runs. Link https://cursor.com/docs/cloud-agent/setup and https://cursor.com/docs/cloud-agent/builds.

## Validation narrower than CI

- Cloud agent checks should be a short path: `pnpm typecheck`, `pnpm lint`, or tests for one package / affected surface.
- Leave the full CI suite (e2e, every workspace package, coverage gates) to PR CI.
- Put that short path in an `AGENTS.md` section titled `Cursor Cloud specific instructions`.

## Secrets

- Never commit secret values. List **names** from `.env.example` and send the user to https://cursor.com/dashboard/cloud-agents (Secrets / environment-scoped secrets).
- Team and environment-scoped secrets are available during Builds; user secrets are not part of the shared snapshot.
